Subject: AlienHand IRC Chat Conversation Refinement

Description: SOP specification for the refined conversation layer that reorganizes raw chat into chapters, bookmarks, notes, sticky references, quotes, and editorial edits without mutating the source conversation record.

@ [source] platform/source/SOP_Markdown.md
@ [source] platform/Delineation.sop
@ [source] platform/Integration.sop
@ [source] platform/Semantic_Refinement.sop
@ [foundation] AlienHand/docs/irc-chat-foundation.md
@ [platform] AlienHand/docs/irc-chat-platform.sop
@ [justification] AlienHand/docs/work-justification.sop

& [AlienHandChatConversationRefinement] is the editorial layer that composes curated conversation views from raw chat history
  + [raw_conversation] is the immutable source chat stream from [AlienHandIRCChatPlatform]
  + [refined_product] is the curated presentation produced from raw conversation segments
  + [chapter] is an editorial grouping of related conversation spans, including discontiguous spans when needed
  + [bookmark] is a reference marker that can attach to raw conversation items and refined chapters
  + [note] is a human or agent annotation attached to a conversation anchor
  + [sticky_reference] is a persistent annotation intended to remain visible across context shifts
  + [quote] is a preserved excerpt with provenance and source identity
  + [editorial_edit] is a transformation applied to the refined product without rewriting the raw source record

  = must: keep raw conversation immutable
  = must: allow chapters to glue together skipped-around exchanges into a coherent editorial narrative
  = must: preserve provenance for every bookmark, note, quote, and sticky reference
  = must: allow bookmarks to exist in both the raw conversation layer and the refined product layer
  = must: keep chapters only in the refined product layer
  = must: allow editorial edits to reshape presentation without erasing source evidence
  - never: treat a chapter as the truth source
  - never: discard raw conversation when generating a refined view

## Layer Boundaries

/ [AlienHandChatConversationRefinement] -(Delineation)> [source_record], [annotation_layer], [refined_layer], [uncertainty]

& [RefinementLayerBoundary] is the separation between raw chat, annotations, and editorialized output
  + [source_record] is the unedited chat substrate and payload history
  + [annotation_layer] is bookmarks, notes, sticky references, and quotes attached to source or refined material
  + [refined_layer] is chapters and post-processed editorial views
  + [uncertainty] is the exact UI treatment of chapter editing, bookmark promotion, and raw/debug visibility

  = must: preserve source record identity in every derived artifact
  = must: allow annotations to point to both raw and refined targets
  = must: keep chapter composition separate from raw transport and replay
  = should: surface raw and refined views side by side when debugging or reviewing

## Identity Vocabulary

| [ConversationArtifactKind] is (raw_message | chapter | bookmark | note | sticky_reference | quote | editorial_edit)
| [RefinedViewMode] is (raw | annotated | chaptered | editorial)
| [BookmarkScope] is (raw_only | refined_only | both)

& [ConversationChapter] is a curated presentation unit for related conversation spans
  + [chapter_id] is a stable identifier for the curated view
  + [title] is the human-readable chapter label
  + [summary] is a concise narrative description of what the chapter contains
  + [members] are the raw message UUIDs or spans included in the chapter
  + [anchors] are bookmarks or reference points used to recover the chapter shape
  + [mode] is [RefinedViewMode]

  = must: support discontiguous grouping when the live conversation skips around
  = must: preserve the source ordering inside each included span
  = must: expose enough metadata for navigation and review

& [ConversationBookmark] is a navigational anchor in either raw or refined conversation space
  + [bookmark_id] is a stable identifier
  + [target] is a raw message, span, or chapter
  + [scope] is [BookmarkScope]
  + [label] is optional human-readable text
  + [note] is optional annotation text attached to the bookmark anchor
  + [note_count] is the number of attached notes

  = must: be attachable to raw conversation items
  = must: be attachable to refined chapters
  = should: survive chapter regeneration when the target still exists

& [ConversationQuote] is a provenance-preserving excerpt
  + [quote_id] is a stable identifier
  + [source_target] is the raw message or chapter source
  + [excerpt] is the preserved text or frame reference
  + [provenance] is source UUID, timestamp, and actor identity

  = must: keep the source reference visible
  = must: not alter the original message record

& [EditorialEdit] is a post-refinement transformation
  + [edit_id] is a stable identifier
  + [input_view] is the chaptered or annotated view being edited
  + [output_view] is the new refined presentation
  + [change_type] is reorder, condense, expand, redact, or annotate

  = must: preserve the original view as evidence
  = must: record the edit as a derivative artifact
  = must: support review of what changed and why

## Presentation Rules

& [RefinedPresentationRules] are the rules for showing refined chat content
  + [normal_view] is the standard chat surface
  + [debug_view] is the raw conversation and annotation surface
  + [chapter_view] is the curated narrative surface
  + [editorial_view] is the post-processed publication surface
  + [user_visible_actions] are inject, remove, bookmark, note, sticky, quote, and toggle views
  + [internal_actions] are chapter regeneration, cut promotion, and edit application
  + [admin_actions] are override, export, and schema repair operations

  = must: keep raw conversation available for inspection
  = must: allow debug view to show source messages, bookmarks, quotes, and edits
  = must: allow normal view to remain simpler than the editorial layer
  = should: let chapter and editorial views coexist without replacing the source
  = must: show command execution text only in raw or debug views when the command itself is part of the record
  = should: suppress routine directive text from the normal conversation view when it is only operational metadata

## Directive Model

& [ConversationDirective] is a structured instruction that changes refinement state rather than ordinary conversation content
  + [directive_id] is the stable identifier
  + [directive_kind] is history_request, create_cut, remove_cut, create_bookmark, add_note, pin_sticky, quote_span, regenerate_chapter, or apply_edit
  + [source] is user action, AI action, or internal system action
  + [payload] is the directive parameters
  + [visibility] is normal, raw_only, debug_only, or internal

  = must: keep directives explicit and auditable
  = must: allow directives to be rendered in raw/debug history without polluting the normal chat story
  = must: support the `!ah history` family while leaving room for UI-driven actions
  = should: permit `=`-prefixed directive notation when a textual directive is emitted

## Split View Editing Model

& [ConversationCutsWorkbench] is the primary refinement UI for composing chapters from live conversation
  + [left_pane] is the raw conversation stream
  + [right_pane] is the cuts view that will become the chaptered/refined product
  + [edits_pane] is the third perspective for editorial transformations
  + [raw_text_toggle] is the control for showing or hiding raw text detail
  + [pane_divider] is the adjustable separator between left and right panes
  + [pointer] is the drag-and-drop insertion target shown in the divider frame and pointing toward the cuts pane

  = must: allow the user to hide or show the raw conversation pane
  = must: allow the user to hide or show the cuts pane
  = must: allow the user to hide or show the edits pane
  = must: hide the divider and pointer whenever either the raw conversation pane or cuts pane is hidden
  = must: keep the divider and pointer visible only when both source and cuts panes are visible
  = must: make the visible panes track together while scrolling when linked
  = must: allow the raw text toggle to independently hide or show raw text detail

& [ConversationCutAction] is the action that promotes one raw conversation block into the cuts pane
  + [source_block] is the raw conversation block selected on the left pane
  + [insertion_point] is the divider pointer location in the cuts pane
  + [remove_button] is the x control on a cut block inside the cuts pane
  + [tracking_mode] is whether the pane scrolls stay linked

  = must: provide a button on each raw conversation block to inject that block into the cuts pane at the insertion point
  = must: render an x control on each cut block so the user can remove it from the cuts perspective
  = must: preserve the raw conversation block when it is added to cuts
  = must: support toggling scroll tracking on and off for the raw text view
  = should: keep the cut set and edit set observable as separate working surfaces

## Frozen Terms

& [ConversationBlock] is one atomic visible unit of live conversation in the raw pane
  + [source] is the underlying message or grouped message span
  + [presentation] is the text, media, or rich payload currently shown to the user
  + [block_id] is the stable identifier for the visible unit
  + [provenance] is the raw message UUIDs and actor identity that produced the block

  = must: represent the smallest practical unit the user can promote into cuts
  = must: remain intact in the raw pane even when copied into cuts
  = should: support text, code, image, link, and mixed payload frames

& [ConversationCut] is a block that has been selected into the cuts pane as part of a refined working set
  + [cut_id] is the stable identifier for the cut instance
  + [source_block] is the original conversation block
  + [position] is the insertion order inside the cuts pane
  + [state] is active or removed_from_cuts

  = must: preserve linkage back to [ConversationBlock]
  = must: be removable from the cuts perspective without destroying the source block
  = must: support reordering as the user refines the narrative

& [ConversationChapter] is the editorial product formed from one or more cuts
  + [chapter_id] is the stable identifier for the chapter
  + [title] is the editorial name for the refined narrative segment
  + [summary] is a concise description of the chapter's intent
  + [members] are the cuts and source spans that compose the chapter

  = must: group related cuts into a coherent presentation artifact
  = must: allow non-contiguous source material when the conversation jumps around
  = must: remain a derivative view rather than replacing the raw stream

& [ConversationEdit] is a transformation applied to a chapter or cuts set
  + [edit_id] is the stable identifier
  + [edit_type] is reorder, condense, expand, redact, annotate, or reframe
  + [input_target] is the chapter or cuts set being edited
  + [output_target] is the revised presentation

  = must: preserve the pre-edit state as evidence
  = must: record the reason for the edit when available
  = must: support review of the before and after forms

& [ConversationBookmark] is a navigational marker that can point into raw or refined conversation
  + [bookmark_id] is the stable identifier
  + [target] is a ConversationBlock, ConversationCut, or ConversationChapter
  + [scope] is raw_only, refined_only, or both
  + [label] is optional human-readable text
  + [note] is optional hover, popup, or annotation text rooted in the same target
  + [persistence] is ephemeral_session or durable_channel
  + [promotion_rule] is how a raw bookmark becomes visible in the refined layer

  = must: help users and agents return to important conversation points
  = must: survive refinement when the target still exists
  = should: be visible in both the raw and editorial interfaces where relevant
  = should: promote to the refined layer when the target becomes part of a chapter or cut set

& [ConversationSticky] is a persistent reference that is intended to remain visible while the session continues
  + [sticky_id] is the stable identifier
  + [target] is a block, cut, chapter, or bookmark
  + [visibility] is visible, collapsed, or hidden
  + [retention] is session-scoped by default
  + [clear_action] is the user or system action that removes the sticky reference

  = must: act as a durable working reminder during refinement
  = must: be easy to surface again when the user returns to the thread
  = should: support pinned constraints, open questions, or standing instructions
  = should: be manually cleared unless a session policy says otherwise

& [ConversationQuote] is a preserved excerpt with explicit source provenance
  + [quote_id] is the stable identifier
  + [source_target] is the originating block, cut, or chapter
  + [excerpt] is the copied text or frame reference
  + [provenance] is the source identity, timestamp, and actor metadata
  + [use_case] is citation, review, comparison, or editorial grounding

  = must: retain exact source traceability
  = must: not mutate the source content
  = should: be usable in both raw review and editorial output

## Schema Model

& [ConversationBlockSchema] is the serializable object model for a raw conversation block
  + [block_id] is the stable identifier
  + [channel_uuid] is the source channel
  + [message_uuid] is the underlying message UUID or message set UUID
  + [sender] is the display or actor identity
  + [sender_type] is user, ai_agent, system, or service
  + [created_at] is the UTC timestamp with milliseconds
  + [payload_kind] is the content classification
  + [presentation] is the rendered summary of the block for the raw pane
  + [raw_refs] is the source reference list for the underlying payloads

  = must: be serializable without requiring chapter or edit state
  = must: be the smallest source-facing object the refinement layer consumes
  = should: preserve enough data to recreate the raw block in the UI

& [ConversationCutSchema] is the serializable object model for a selected cut
  + [cut_id] is the stable identifier
  + [source_block_id] is the linked raw block
  + [position] is the ordering within the cuts pane
  + [status] is active, removed, or superseded
  + [annotations] are bookmarks, notes, quotes, or sticky references attached to the cut

  = must: preserve a backlink to [ConversationBlockSchema]
  = must: not rewrite the underlying raw block
  = should: support drag-and-drop reordering and removal

& [ConversationChapterSchema] is the serializable object model for a refined chapter
  + [chapter_id] is the stable identifier
  + [title] is the editorial label
  + [summary] is the chapter-level synopsis
  + [member_cut_ids] are the contributing cut identifiers
  + [member_block_ids] are the contributing raw block identifiers
  + [bookmarks] are the chapter-visible bookmark objects
  + [quotes] are the chapter-visible quote objects
  + [edit_chain] is the ordered list of edits applied to the chapter

  = must: represent a derived artifact, not the source record
  = must: preserve provenance back to the contributing cuts and blocks
  = should: be regenerable from the source and cut history

& [ConversationEditSchema] is the serializable object model for an editorial transformation
  + [edit_id] is the stable identifier
  + [input_ref] is the chapter or cuts set being transformed
  + [output_ref] is the resulting chapter or refined artifact
  + [edit_type] is reorder, condense, expand, redact, annotate, or reframe
  + [reason] is the optional explanation for the edit
  + [author] is the user, AI, or system that produced the edit

  = must: preserve the input state for review
  = must: preserve lineage from input to output
  = should: serialize as a change record that can be replayed or inspected

& [ConversationBookmarkSchema] is the serializable object model for a bookmark
  + [bookmark_id] is the stable identifier
  + [target_ref] is the raw block, cut, or chapter reference
  + [scope] is raw_only, refined_only, or both
  + [label] is optional display text
  + [note] is optional annotation text that follows the bookmark across raw and refined layers
  + [persistence] is ephemeral_session or durable_channel
  + [promotion_state] is raw, promoted, mirrored, or retired

  = must: support both raw and refined targets
  = must: preserve enough target identity to survive regeneration when possible
  = should: be safe to store as a light reference object

& [ConversationStickySchema] is the serializable object model for a sticky reference
  + [sticky_id] is the stable identifier
  + [target_ref] is the block, cut, chapter, or bookmark reference
  + [visibility] is visible, collapsed, or hidden
  + [retention] is session-scoped by default
  + [clear_state] is active, dismissed, or expired

  = must: act as a persistent working reminder
  = must: be removable without mutating the target
  = should: serialize independently from the target content

& [ConversationQuoteSchema] is the serializable object model for a quote
  + [quote_id] is the stable identifier
  + [source_ref] is the block, cut, or chapter reference
  + [excerpt] is the quoted text or frame reference
  + [provenance] is the source identity metadata
  + [display_mode] is inline, block, or anchored

  = must: keep exact source traceability
  = must: remain a derivative view, not a content mutation
  = should: be easy to render in raw, chaptered, or editorial views

## Storage Model

& [ConversationStorageModel] is the durable local persistence contract for the refinement layer
  + [database] is SQLite as the canonical local store for raw conversation, cuts, chapters, annotations, edits, and indexes
  + [raw_table] stores raw conversation block schema rows
  + [cut_table] stores selected cut rows and their ordering
  + [chapter_table] stores chapter rows and chapter metadata
  + [bookmark_table] stores bookmarks and mirrored bookmarks
  + [sticky_table] stores sticky references
  + [quote_table] stores quote records
  + [edit_table] stores edit records or references to edit diff artifacts
  + [toc_table] stores the chapter and edit table of contents
  + [search_index_table] stores token and term-to-block mappings

  = must: keep raw conversation, cuts, bookmarks, chapters, and edits queryable through one local database
  = must: support search/indexing against terms that map back to the raw block that contains them
  = must: support a table of contents for the edit layer
  = should: keep derivable views linked by stable IDs rather than by duplicated content

& [ConversationSQLiteStorageV1] is the first implemented SQLite storage contract for refinement data
  + [implementation] is AlienHand/python/alienhand_ai/refinement_storage.py
  + [proof_command] is chat-refinement-storage-proof
  + [schema_version] is 1
  + [migration_table] is schema_migrations
  + [serialized_json_fields] are tuple, reference, metadata, provenance, source scope, and diff content fields stored as canonical JSON text

  = must: migrate deterministically to [schema_version]
  = must: persist blocks, cuts, chapters, bookmarks, stickies, quotes, edits, edit diffs, TOC entries, and search terms
  = must: keep search terms mapped back to source block IDs
  = must: support user-driven block-to-cut-to-chapter-to-edit proof flow
  = should: treat future storage revisions as additive migrations

& [ConversationReplayImportV1] is the first bridge from durable chat replay into refinement storage
  + [implementation] is AlienHand/python/alienhand_ai/refinement_storage.py import_replay_rows
  + [proof_command] is chat-refinement-replay-proof
  + [source] is [ChannelJSONLHistory] plus [PayloadStore] replay rows
  + [target] is [ConversationBlockSchema] rows in [ConversationSQLiteStorageV1]
  + [block_id_rule] is "message:<message_uuid>"

  = must: import resolved replay payloads into searchable conversation blocks
  = must: skip payload_error rows by default
  = must: be idempotent for repeated replay imports of the same message UUIDs
  = must: preserve raw history and payload references in block metadata
  = should: let imported blocks seed user-controlled cuts and chapters

& [AppOwnedRefinementStorageLifecycle] is the app service ownership path for live refinement storage
  + [implementation] is AlienHand/python/alienhand_ai/chat_platform.py AlienHandChatService refinement store fields
  + [proof_command] is chat-app-refinement-proof
  + [live_ingest] is app publication immediately upserting the published payload into [ConversationSQLiteStorageV1]
  + [cold_sync] is rebuilding refinement blocks from [ConversationReplayImportV1]
  + [source_of_truth] remains JSONL history plus payload files

  = must: keep the refinement SQLite database app-owned
  = must: ingest newly published app messages into refinement blocks
  = must: close the refinement store with app service shutdown
  = must: allow cold replay sync to rebuild refinement blocks from durable chat history
  = should: treat refinement storage as derived state that can be recovered from source history

& [ConversationRefinementHTTPV1] is the local authenticated HTTP API for the future split-pane workbench
  + [implementation] is AlienHand/python/alienhand_ai/payload_http.py refinement routes
  + [proof_command] is chat-refinement-http-proof
  + [base_path] is /alienhand/refinement
  + [auth] is the prototype bearer token shared with [PayloadResolverHTTP]
  + [read_endpoints] are blocks, search, cuts, chapters, and bookmarks
  + [write_endpoints] are create cut, remove cut, create chapter, and create bookmark

  = must: expose channel-filtered conversation blocks for the raw pane
  = must: expose search hits that map terms back to source block IDs
  = must: expose channel-filtered cuts and chapters when a channel UUID is supplied
  = must: expose channel-filtered bookmarks and bookmark notes when a channel UUID is supplied
  = must: allow explicit user-controlled creation of cuts from source blocks
  = must: allow explicit user-controlled soft-removal of cuts
  = must: allow explicit user-controlled chapter creation from selected cuts
  = must: allow explicit user-controlled creation of bookmark notes against source blocks, cuts, or chapters
  = must: reject bookmark creation when the requested target anchor does not exist
  = must: reject unauthenticated refinement reads and writes when a resolver token is configured
  = should: remain a narrow workbench contract until richer UI behavior is implemented

& [ConversationBookmarkHTTPV1] is the first runtime contract for bookmark-attached notes
  + [implementation] is AlienHand/python/alienhand_ai/refinement_storage.py create_bookmark and list_bookmarks
  + [implementation] is AlienHand/python/alienhand_ai/payload_http.py /alienhand/refinement/bookmarks
  + [target_types] are block, cut, and chapter
  + [note_root] is the target conversation anchor
  + [channel_filter] resolves bookmarks through the channel membership of the target block, cut source block, or chapter member blocks

  = must: preserve the bookmark note as part of the bookmark object
  = must: list bookmarks by channel so raw and refined panes can show the same anchor
  = must: list bookmarks by target type when the UI only needs one layer
  = must: validate that the target block, cut, or chapter exists before inserting the bookmark
  = should: support later hover and popup note presentation without changing the storage object

& [TheLoungeRefinementWorkbenchV1] is the first browser-facing refinement workbench in the AlienHand The Lounge fork
  + [implementation] is AlienHand/thelounge/client/components/AlienHandRefinementWorkbench.vue
  + [helper] is AlienHand/thelounge/client/js/helpers/alienhand.ts refinement API helpers
  + [style] is AlienHand/thelounge/client/css/alienhand-chat.css workbench styling
  + [entrypoint] is AlienHand/thelounge/client/components/Chat.vue Cuts toggle
  + [proof_command] is chat-workbench-runtime-proof
  + [fork_commit] is 9252cb34

  = must: appear only for channel names that resolve to a 32-character hexadecimal UUID
  = must: provide a visible Cuts control at the top chat frame
  = must: fetch raw conversation blocks for the current channel
  = must: search raw blocks through [ConversationRefinementHTTPV1]
  = must: let a user inject a raw block into the cuts pane
  = must: let a user remove an active cut with an x control
  = must: let a user create a chapter from the active channel cuts
  = must: expose a raw JSON/debug view for the workbench state
  = should: keep this first UI slice intentionally rough until runtime interaction is reviewed
  ? [not_yet_done] is adjustable divider, drag pointer motion, bookmark hover notes, quote controls, and polished editorial edit UI

& [TheLoungeRefinementWorkbenchRuntimeProof] is the app-owned runtime verification for the first refinement workbench
  + [implementation] is AlienHand/python/alienhand_ai/payload_http.py run_app_thelounge_refinement_workbench_proof
  + [proof_command] is chat-workbench-runtime-proof
  + [runtime_group] is one local Ergo server, one payload resolver, one The Lounge process, and one UUID-named channel
  + [bundle_check] verifies The Lounge serves the workbench client bundle and style sheet
  + [api_check] verifies the app-owned resolver can list blocks, search, create a cut, create a chapter, and remove a cut

  = must: start and stop the app-owned runtime group
  = must: publish a real app message into a UUID channel
  = must: resolve that message through the payload resolver
  = must: verify the channel block is available through [ConversationRefinementHTTPV1]
  = must: verify The Lounge serves workbench code and styling
  = should: remain a runtime smoke test until browser-level click automation is added

& [TheLoungeRefinementWorkbenchLiveReview] is the manual/browser review launcher for the first refinement workbench
  + [implementation] is AlienHand/python/alienhand_ai/cli.py chat-workbench-live
  + [ready_file] is a JSON document containing app ports, resolver URL, The Lounge URL, channel UUID, IRC channel, and seeded message UUID
  + [stop_file] is an optional file path that ends the live runtime when created
  + [fallback_stop] is Ctrl+C when no stop file is supplied

  = must: start the same app-owned runtime group as [TheLoungeRefinementWorkbenchRuntimeProof]
  = must: publish one seeded message into a UUID-named channel
  = must: keep the runtime alive for browser or human review
  = must: write review connection details before waiting
  = must: shut down Ergo, payload resolver, and The Lounge when review ends
  = should: support automated harnesses through ready-file and stop-file paths

& [ConversationEditDiffArtifact] is the change record for an editorial edit
  + [diff_id] is the stable identifier
  + [edit_id] is the parent edit identifier
  + [source_ref] is the raw, cut, or chapter object the diff applies to
  + [diff_format] is a structured diff or patch representation
  + [diff_uri] is the database or file reference to the diff artifact

  = must: allow edits to be referenced through the database in the same way raw objects are referenced
  = must: preserve the before and after relationship for review
  = should: remain small enough to support audit and regeneration

& [ConversationSearchIndexSchema] is the serializable object model for indexed search terms
  + [term] is the normalized search token
  + [block_id] is the raw block that contains the term
  + [offset] is the token or character position when available
  + [chapter_id] is the optional chapter reference when the term is surfaced in a refined view
  + [cut_id] is the optional cut reference when the term is surfaced in the cuts view

  = must: map terms back to the message block where the term is found
  = must: support navigation from search result to source block
  = should: support later expansion into chapter and edit search if needed

& [ConversationTableOfContentsSchema] is the serializable object model for the refined layer navigation outline
  + [toc_id] is the stable identifier
  + [toc_type] is chapter, edit, or mixed
  + [entries] are ordered references to chapters, edits, or both
  + [source_scope] is the set of raw blocks or cuts covered by the entry

  = must: provide navigation for the chapter layer and the edit layer
  = must: preserve display order as an explicit object, not inferred UI state
  = should: support collapse, expand, and jump navigation

## User Control State

& [ConversationRefinementState] is the user-driven state machine for moving raw conversation into refined products
  + [raw_selected] is a raw block currently selected in the left pane
  + [cut_selected] is a raw block copied into the cuts pane
  + [chapter_composed] is a cut set organized into a chapter
  + [bookmark_mirrored] is a bookmark visible in both source and refined layers
  + [sticky_pinned] is a persistent reference remaining visible during the session
  + [edit_applied] is an editorial transformation recorded against a chapter or cut set

  = must: make state changes user-controlled through explicit buttons or direct UI actions
  = must: support raw-selected to cut-selected, cut-selected to chapter-composed, and chapter-composed to edit-applied transitions
  = must: keep bookmark mirroring visible on both source and refined layers
  = must: allow notes to persist by being attached to the original anchor and echoed into derived views
  = should: avoid implicit promotion when an explicit user action is the desired source of truth

& [ConversationAnnotationSemantics] is the behavior contract for bookmark, note, sticky, and quote usage
  + [bookmark] is the anchor
  + [note] is the attached explanation, hover text, or annotation payload
  + [sticky] is a bookmark-like annotation that remains visible until cleared
  + [quote] is the exact preserved excerpt used for citation or comparison

  = must: mirror bookmarks into refined views where the source remains relevant
  = must: attach notes to the original conversation anchor and echo them into refined views
  = must: allow hover or popup presentation of notes in the UI
  = must: highlight bookmarked source blocks
  = should: remove the need for a separate Notes feature by treating notes as bookmark-attached annotations
